In "Ai12_CaptureMessageImage", we read the chart's pixel size, clamp it to between 320 by 240 and 4096 by 4096, and temporarily hide the panel canvases so the screenshot contains only the chart. Under a unique base name, we save two copies, a
Portable Network Graphics
(PNG) for the request and archive and a
BMP
for showing in the panel, restore the panel at once, and read the PNG back through the encoder so we hand the caller both the base64 and the native width and height. Since capturing does nothing on its own until a message wants it, we next stage the shot as a pending attachment.
Staging and Removing the Attachment
Behind the new "Chart Screenshot" footer action sits a small piece of state and two actions that fill and clear it.
